#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068487 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c22b8e9-049a-5574-86c9-35788c410421" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Binomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/id #uuid "fd2d4aca-7859-5bed-a514-43d82ba25400" :question/math-academy-id "e-4102" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{2x+3}{(x^2+4)(x-1)} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The quadratic factor $x^2+4$ is irreducible, so we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+3}{({x}^{2}+4)(x-1)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}+4)}+\\frac{C}{(x-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x^2+4)(x-1),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+3 & =(Ax+B)(x-1)+C({x}^{2}+4)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=-1, B=1,$ and $C=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x+3}{(x^2+4)(x-1)} = \\dfrac{-x+1}{x^2+4} +\\dfrac{1}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nNow we integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+3}{({x}^{2}+4)(x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{-x+1}{{x}^{2}+4}+\\frac{1}{x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution $u = x^2+4.$ Then $2x\\,\\textrm{d}x=\\textrm{d}u,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral,  we use the fact that $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{x^2+a^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x = \\dfrac{1}{a}\\arctan\\left(\\dfrac{x}{a}\\right),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+3}{({x}^{2}+4)(x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068513 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Trinomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/id #uuid "3a2e21bb-c966-5429-98c0-9af209c45dfe" :question/math-academy-id "e-510" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{4x^2-x}{(x^2+x+1)(x-2)} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a negative discriminant:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{D} = 1^2 - 4(1)(1) = -3 < 0\n$$\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{2}-x}{({x}^{2}+x+1)(x-2)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+x+1}+\\frac{C}{x-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x^2+x+1)(x-2)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-x & =(Ax+B)(x-2)+C({x}^{2}+x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get  $A=2,$ $B=1,$ and $C=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4x^2-x}{(x^2+x+1)(x-2)} = \\dfrac{2x+1}{x^2+x+1} + \\dfrac{2}{x-2}.\n$$\n\nNow we integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration only at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}-x}{({x}^{2}+x+1)(x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x+1}+\\frac{2}{x-2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x+1}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution $u = x^2+x+1.$ Then $(2x+1) \\, \\textrm{d}x=\\textrm{d}u,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+x+1| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}-x}{({x}^{2}+x+1)(x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x+1}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+x+1)+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068571 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a78860ea-192f-5df9-aca9-4f67ec6ffefe" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Given Part Of the Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/id #uuid "8168f846-013a-529a-a916-501438b2ca30" :question/math-academy-id "e-7316" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4x^2-6}{(x-3)(x^2+1)} = \\dfrac{A}{x-3} + \\dfrac{x+3}{x^2 + 1},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant to be found, calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{4x^2-6}{(x-3)(x^2+1)}\\,\\textrm d x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the constant $A.$ Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-3)(x^2 + 1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-6=A({x}^{2}+1)+{x}^{2}-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=0$  into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2}-6 & =A({0}^{2}+1)+{0}^{2}-9 \\\\ -6 & =A-9 \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\int \\dfrac{4x^2 - 6}{(x-3)(x^2+1)} \\, \\textrm{d}x & = \\int \\left(\\dfrac{3}{x-3} + \\dfrac{x+3}{x^2 + 1}\\right) \\textrm{d}x \\[5pt]\n\n& = 3\\int\\dfrac{1}{x-3}\\,\\textrm{d}x + \\int \\dfrac{x}{x^2+1}\\,\\textrm d x + 3\\int \\dfrac{1}{x^2 + 1} \\, \\textrm{d}x\n\t}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{x-3} \\textrm{d}x = \\ln|x-3|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $x^2 + 1 = u.$ Then, $2x\\,\\textrm{d}x=\\textrm{d}u,$ and we get \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\int \\dfrac{x}{x^2+1}\\,\\textrm{d}x & = \\int \\left(\\dfrac{1}{u}\\right) \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{2} \\[5pt]\n\n&= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\ln \\vert u\\vert \\[5pt]\n\n&= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\ln \\vert x^2 + 1\\vert \\[5pt]\n\n& = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\ln \\left(x^2+1\\right).\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n}\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we use the fact that $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{x^2 + a^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x = \\dfrac{1}{a}\\arctan\\left(\\dfrac{x}{a}\\right),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{x^2+1}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\arctan{x}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}-6}{(x-3)({x}^{2}+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)+3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c22b8e9-049a-5574-86c9-35788c410421" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Binomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b37dc6c-46f6-5a0a-9532-6ec2d83e71b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+9)+\\frac{5}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{9})+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318451} {:answer/id #uuid "141b6ee6-1e72-5470-9df9-76c3398802d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+9)+\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318452} {:answer/id #uuid "7e922e5c-6aed-576c-8775-a3ec68bb10aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+9)-\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318453} {:answer/id #uuid "604953a1-e49a-5205-914a-89eac2da3602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+9)-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318454} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2aaaec-54d3-5584-9bad-723d2cbef074" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+9)+\\frac{5}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{9})+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e922e5c-6aed-576c-8775-a3ec68bb10aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+9)-\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318453} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cabb580-b646-52ed-a271-e4eef28927e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4be761bf-2e3f-59dc-aa50-0d26eafc28a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-11359" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x+42}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The quadratic factor ${x}^{2}+9$ is irreducible, so we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+42}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-3)}=\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+9}+\\frac{C}{x-3}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $({x}^{2}+9)(x-3),$ and we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+x+42=(Ax+B)(x-3)+C({x}^{2}+9).\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=-2,B=-5,$ and $C=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+42}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-3)}=-\\frac{2x+5}{{x}^{2}+9}+\\frac{3}{x-3}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x+42}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{2x+5}{{x}^{2}+9}+\\frac{3}{x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+9}\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+9}\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use a substitution $u={x}^{2}+9.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+9| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}).\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x+42}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+9}\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+9}\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+9)-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+9)-\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318456 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a78860ea-192f-5df9-aca9-4f67ec6ffefe" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Given Part Of the Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03c8854a-2ae2-53b8-81ce-9bf6c2e5dd9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+5)-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318458} {:answer/id #uuid "754ce348-18b4-52ef-829c-b02d61ef635e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{5})-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318459} {:answer/id #uuid "8737a2c6-a9aa-5911-ad39-1f9b35496c34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+5)+\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{5})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318460} {:answer/id #uuid "d2b7840a-5fc4-58d2-bae2-8607a609af80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+5)+\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{5})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318461} {:answer/id #uuid "22f2512c-d97d-529a-bac5-365bb26452b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+5)-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2b7840a-5fc4-58d2-bae2-8607a609af80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+5)+\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{5})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318461} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c2bf9fc-b37f-5364-a46e-3830d4378a8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22d2cf0d-6a1f-51ae-9a19-1da4f559ff4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-115665" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+5x-2}{(x+1)({x}^{2}+5)}=\\frac{2x+B}{{x}^{2}+5}-\\frac{1}{x+1},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is a constant to be found, calculate $\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+5x-2}{(x+1)({x}^{2}+5)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the constant $B.$ Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+1)({x}^{2}+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5x-2 & =(2x+B)(x+1)-({x}^{2}+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=0$  into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}+5(0)-2 & =(2(0)+B)(0+1)-({0}^{2}+5) \\\\ -2 & =B-5 \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+5x-2}{(x+1)({x}^{2}+5)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2x+3}{{x}^{2}+5}-\\frac{1}{x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+5}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+5}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution ${x}^{2}+5=u.$ Then, $2x\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u,$ and we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{5}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+5x-2}{(x+1)({x}^{2}+5)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+5)+\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{5})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318463 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a78860ea-192f-5df9-aca9-4f67ec6ffefe" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Given Part Of the Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f1ecb0d-0399-52ab-a62d-315391c309ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+8)-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}x}{4})+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318465} {:answer/id #uuid "ae1a1bab-1a1d-5c37-8e9f-706949081d57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+8)+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}x}{4})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318466} {:answer/id #uuid "30313cb9-4807-589f-adb5-49c32d60452b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+8)+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}x}{4})+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318467} {:answer/id #uuid "d0877862-090a-5734-8794-33d7bc5cb9b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+8)-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}x}{4})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318468} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ea5096-99ab-59b4-bd7f-7b1756d19fee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+8)-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}x}{4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f1ecb0d-0399-52ab-a62d-315391c309ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+8)-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}x}{4})+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318465} :answer-field/id #uuid "4901cd59-b982-5f19-8048-6bc3c145473e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "54ca2bf3-93df-5c2d-b960-dcf266a17a72" :question/math-academy-id "q-115667" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}+20}{(x+2)({x}^{2}+8)}=\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}+8}+\\frac{D}{x+2},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant to be found, calculate $\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+20}{(x+2)({x}^{2}+8)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the constant $D.$ Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+2)({x}^{2}+8)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+20 & =(x-2)(x+2)+D({x}^{2}+8).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=0$  into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2}+20 & =(0-2)(0+2)+D({0}^{2}+8) \\\\ 20 & =-4+8D \\\\ 24 & =8D \\\\ D & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+20}{(x+2)({x}^{2}+8)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}+8}+\\frac{3}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution ${x}^{2}+8=u.$ Then, $x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+8).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}x}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we get\n\n$$\n3\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\text{d}x=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+20}{(x+2)({x}^{2}+8)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+8)-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}x}{4})+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318470 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a78860ea-192f-5df9-aca9-4f67ec6ffefe" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Given Part Of the Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc3a26c9-2e5d-52e9-8485-d4699dd94d3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+20)-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{10}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{10})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318472} {:answer/id #uuid "b6902573-e6c8-5939-9f76-e3041d410cf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+20)-\\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{10}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{10})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318473} {:answer/id #uuid "b6bda6d8-7ae6-5717-b311-15cdccf5b73c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+20)-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318474} {:answer/id #uuid "88304b7f-29e2-55ca-83b2-792a0abbdb1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+20)+\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{10})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318475} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a240cf-ad4e-5be8-bc68-6a5544397cad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+20)-\\frac{7}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6902573-e6c8-5939-9f76-e3041d410cf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+20)-\\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{10}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{10})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318473} :answer-field/id #uuid "2af59726-f807-57a6-a169-19d400837bd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5210bbf7-af3e-55cd-8b4b-05a1e7890ac8" :question/math-academy-id "q-115673" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-5x-27}{(x+1)({x}^{2}+20)}=\\frac{2x+B}{{x}^{2}+20}-\\frac{1}{x+1},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is a constant to be found, calculate $\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}-5x-27}{(x+1)({x}^{2}+20)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the constant $B.$ Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+1)({x}^{2}+20)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-5x-27 & =(2x+B)(x+1)-({x}^{2}+20).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=0$  into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}-5(0)-27 & =(2(0)+B)(0+1)-({0}^{2}+20) \\\\ -27 & =B-20 \\\\ B & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}-5x-27}{(x+1)({x}^{2}+20)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2x-7}{{x}^{2}+20}-\\frac{1}{x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+20}\\,\\text{d}x-7\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+20}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution ${x}^{2}+20=u.$ Then, $2x\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u,$ and we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+20}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+20).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+20}\\,\\text{d}x & =7\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+(2\\sqrt{5})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{5}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{10}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{10}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}-5x-27}{(x+1)({x}^{2}+20)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+20)-\\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{10}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{10})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318477 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c22b8e9-049a-5574-86c9-35788c410421" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Binomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3180b8fb-cf79-5e85-a7be-8daf43405ce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+6)-\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{6}})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318479} {:answer/id #uuid "89ff1a81-7fcf-52a3-aac6-419cfc193d28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+6)-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{6}})+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318480} {:answer/id #uuid "22f095e4-c340-5a24-b438-be13e9caf9f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+6)-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{6}})-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318481} {:answer/id #uuid "2e0ec728-0aff-5098-9cb7-23c47cf76585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+6)-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{6}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{6}})+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318482} {:answer/id #uuid "cdf91f96-d176-5bc4-aeb8-793194dbce8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+6)-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{6}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{6}})-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdf91f96-d176-5bc4-aeb8-793194dbce8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+6)-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{6}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{6}})-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318483} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b603f35-c21b-528c-a7be-88a8542dd4df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "52162f56-cb6d-5e9a-b024-198adb3548c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-115690" :question/problem "Find the integral of $\\frac{-{x}^{2}-7x}{({x}^{2}+6)(x-3)}.$" :question/worked-solution "The quadratic factor ${x}^{2}+6$ is irreducible, so we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}^{2}-7x}{({x}^{2}+6)(x-3)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+6}+\\frac{C}{x-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $({x}^{2}+6)(x-3),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-7x & =(Ax+B)(x-3)+C({x}^{2}+6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=1,B=-4,$ and $C=-2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}^{2}-7x}{({x}^{2}+6)(x-3)} & =\\frac{x-4}{{x}^{2}+6}-\\frac{2}{x-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-{x}^{2}-7x}{({x}^{2}+6)(x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{x-4}{{x}^{2}+6}-\\frac{2}{x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+6}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+6}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}+6.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+6| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+6}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{6}}).\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-{x}^{2}-7x}{({x}^{2}+6)(x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+6}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+6}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+6)-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{6}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{6}})-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318484 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c22b8e9-049a-5574-86c9-35788c410421" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Binomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bced6a2-4069-5565-ab11-f6a547bba2c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3)-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}x}{3})+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318486} {:answer/id #uuid "d99a3969-6f80-571b-b38b-d7be6153df22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3)-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}x}{3})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318487} {:answer/id #uuid "0d30f041-ea27-5910-824b-64bfed077fcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3)-3\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}x}{3})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318488} {:answer/id #uuid "a969888d-aea4-5de2-8c73-93b1e5653e1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3)-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}x}{3})+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318489} {:answer/id #uuid "65729765-52c1-50a4-80fe-fb8b2d778277" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3)+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}x}{3})+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d99a3969-6f80-571b-b38b-d7be6153df22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3)-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}x}{3})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318487} :answer-field/id #uuid "feb346dc-a966-5c06-b7b1-1c00b315e656" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4704b6d1-ced4-515d-b46b-469c3c8c9b81" :question/math-academy-id "q-115693" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+5x-9}{({x}^{2}+3)(x+4)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The quadratic factor ${x}^{2}+3$ is irreducible, so we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}+5x-9}{({x}^{2}+3)(x+4)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+3}+\\frac{C}{x+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $({x}^{2}+3)(x+4),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+5x-9 & =(Ax+B)(x+4)+C({x}^{2}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=2,B=-3,$ and $C=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}+5x-9}{({x}^{2}+3)(x+4)} & =\\frac{2x-3}{{x}^{2}+3}+\\frac{1}{x+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+5x-9}{({x}^{2}+3)(x+4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2x-3}{{x}^{2}+3}+\\frac{1}{x+4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}+3.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+3| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}x}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+5x-9}{({x}^{2}+3)(x+4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3)-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}x}{3})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318491 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Trinomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7e1adeb-ca1b-5159-bb12-47bba6197129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2{x}^{2}+5x-6|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318493} {:answer/id #uuid "537e5d9f-8604-501f-978d-e38edaf7e71f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{2{x}^{2}+5x-6}{3}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318494} {:answer/id #uuid "f711bc6c-442c-5ceb-a5de-7e51f570e282" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2{x}^{2}+5x-6|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318495} {:answer/id #uuid "2aa0caa2-c597-5440-a59c-361084327b1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2{x}^{2}+5x-6|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318496} {:answer/id #uuid "2de97c72-8af9-59b2-8fe4-b3b9ad35f875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2{x}^{2}+5x-6|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2aa0caa2-c597-5440-a59c-361084327b1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2{x}^{2}+5x-6|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318496} :answer-field/id #uuid "485e7d1e-e8f2-5b96-915a-21a0623c63a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318492}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "af3a2a5c-cebe-5ef0-9ec4-83831d0e4bc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-115712" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral  $\\int \\frac{12-5x}{x(2{x}^{2}+5x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a discriminant that is not a perfect square:\n\n$$\nD=(5)^{2}-4(2)(-6)=73\n$$\n\nWe have that $\\sqrt{73}$ is not a rational number, which implies that the quadratic factor doesn't factor over the rational numbers.\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12-5x}{x(2{x}^{2}+5x-6)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{Bx+C}{2{x}^{2}+5x-6}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $x(2{x}^{2}+5x-6),$ and we get\n\n$$\n12-5x=A(2{x}^{2}+5x-6)+(Bx+C)x\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=-2,B=4$, and $C=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{12-5x}{x(2{x}^{2}+5x-6)}=-\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{4x+5}{2{x}^{2}+5x-6}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{12-5x}{x(2{x}^{2}+5x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{4x+5}{2{x}^{2}+5x-6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{4x+5}{2{x}^{2}+5x-6}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u=2{x}^{2}+5x-6.$ Then $\\text{d}u=(4x+5)\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4x+5}{2{x}^{2}+5x-6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2{x}^{2}+5x-6|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{12-5x}{x(2{x}^{2}+5x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{4x+5}{2{x}^{2}+5x-6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2{x}^{2}+5x-6|+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318498 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c22b8e9-049a-5574-86c9-35788c410421" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Binomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77547056-a867-5c74-8269-21e7cb2fefac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318500} {:answer/id #uuid "8dd9ab62-cb1b-5906-9ad8-12f19f154a54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+\\frac{4}{x+4}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318501} {:answer/id #uuid "53b91e1a-066b-5fe0-9881-8134779a60b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318502} {:answer/id #uuid "75cebb3f-be25-53fe-a6f5-9a4f92a9e2cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318503} {:answer/id #uuid "28d8f2fa-14d4-5df6-b5e3-8ac95c5e6f27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|-\\frac{1}{x+4}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75cebb3f-be25-53fe-a6f5-9a4f92a9e2cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318503} :answer-field/id #uuid "093a904a-682e-5e33-ac92-01c8fe509d37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d6c4096b-de01-5b1a-9850-164fb16df37c" :question/math-academy-id "q-3614" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x+12}{(x-2)({x}^{2}+4)}.$" :question/worked-solution "The quadratic factor ${x}^{2}+4$ is irreducible, so we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x+12}{(x-2)({x}^{2}+4)}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{Bx+C}{{x}^{2}+4}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-2)({x}^{2}+4),$ and we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+4x+12=A({x}^{2}+4)+(Bx+C)(x-2).\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=3,B=-2,$ and $C=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x+12}{(x-2)({x}^{2}+4)} & =\\frac{3}{x-2}+\\frac{-2x+0}{{x}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{x-2}-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+4x+12}{(x-2)({x}^{2}+4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{3}{x-2}-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|.\n$$\n\n             \n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}+4.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+4x+12}{(x-2)({x}^{2}+4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4)+K\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Trinomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12eb189d-c7a9-5bea-a55d-bda1da7877c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-1|+\\frac{2}{x-1}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318507} {:answer/id #uuid "7c08ac80-a572-5ed2-909e-30c317180a39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318508} {:answer/id #uuid "5018be78-575a-562b-8a80-f76d28e1a8ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-1|+\\frac{1}{2x-2}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318509} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf64316-5423-55f3-9018-5bd33ae54b33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318510} {:answer/id #uuid "aacbe586-a2ed-5e85-bb58-a5829427125a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-1|+\\frac{2}{x-1}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c08ac80-a572-5ed2-909e-30c317180a39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318508} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bfbf8d8-2a30-59f3-ba5e-92afc6da6695" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318506}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1fe5cbae-2a7d-564c-a67e-5f8a767a62df" :question/math-academy-id "q-3617" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+9x-4}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+4x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a discriminant that is not a perfect square:\n\n$$\nD={4}^{2}-4(1)(-1)=20\n$$\n\nWe have that $\\sqrt{20}$ is not a rational number, which implies that the quadratic factor doesn't factor over the rational numbers.\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}+9x-4}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+4x-1)}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{Bx+C}{{x}^{2}+4x-1}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-1)({x}^{2}+4x-1),$ and we get\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}+9x-4=A({x}^{2}+4x-1)+(Bx+C)(x-1)\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=2,B=1$ and $C=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}+9x-4}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+4x-1)}=\\frac{2}{x-1}+\\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}+4x-1}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+9x-4}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+4x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x-1}+\\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}+4x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}+4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n2\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}+4x-1.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2(x+2)\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}+4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-1|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+9x-4}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+4x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}+4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-1|+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Trinomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b331f0cd-7c65-5331-9813-e2eb0f9e654e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\ln \\mid x - 4 \\mid - \\frac{2}{5}\\ln (2x^{2} - 6x + 9) + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066792} {:answer/id #uuid "ddba0abc-0dbf-5883-a45a-f557fa2088f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\ln (2x^{2} - 6x + 9) - 5\\ln \\mid x - 4 \\mid + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066793} {:answer/id #uuid "2a79e75f-f0bd-557c-9790-a0eb98965684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25\\ln (2x^{2} - 6x + 9) - 10\\ln \\mid x - 4 \\mid + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066794} {:answer/id #uuid "37c5a9d6-9f08-56b2-8223-ff8124e1036b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\ln (2x^{2} - 6x + 9) - 5\\ln \\mid x - 4 \\mid + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066795} {:answer/id #uuid "4db1d312-bf1d-58d6-aeef-da61ae6c5d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\ln \\mid x - 4 \\mid + \\frac{2}{5}\\ln (2x^{2} - 6x + 9) + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37c5a9d6-9f08-56b2-8223-ff8124e1036b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\ln (2x^{2} - 6x + 9) - 5\\ln \\mid x - 4 \\mid + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066795} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff70e0fb-103a-5176-9ccc-a563f1b3edb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "731b8f94-fb6c-56e8-9abe-5ac794eb1b1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-3638" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int \\frac{15-25x}{(2{x}^{2}-6x+9)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a negative discriminant:\n\n$$\nD=(-6)^{2}-4(2)(9)=-36<0\n$$\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{15-25x}{(2{x}^{2}-6x+9)(x-4)}=\\frac{Ax+B}{2{x}^{2}-6x+9}+\\frac{C}{x-4}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(2{x}^{2}-6x+9)(x-4),$ and we get\n\n$$\n15-25x=(Ax+B)(x-4)+C(2{x}^{2}-6x+9).\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=10,B=-15$ and $C=-5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{15-25x}{(2{x}^{2}-6x+9)(x-4)}=\\frac{10x-15}{2{x}^{2}-6x+9}+\\frac{-5}{x-4}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{15-25x}{(2{x}^{2}-6x+9)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{10x-15}{2{x}^{2}-6x+9}+\\frac{-5}{x-4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{2x-3}{2{x}^{2}-6x+9}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution $u=2{x}^{2}-6x+9.$ Then $\\text{d}u=(4x-6)\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x-3}{2{x}^{2}-6x+9}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2{x}^{2}-6x+9| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{2}-6x+9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{15-25x}{(2{x}^{2}-6x+9)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\frac{2x-3}{2{x}^{2}-6x+9}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{2}-6x+9))-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{2}-6x+9)-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318512 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Trinomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42315802-ccfa-5c5f-9ce9-b556dac278e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+x+1)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318514} {:answer/id #uuid "502b1cd2-df63-522e-9f6e-3280bcbea7d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+x+1)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318515} {:answer/id #uuid "34076c30-ce7f-5a4d-9ffc-abc625def11f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+x+1)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318516} {:answer/id #uuid "decb3d07-4b90-53c5-bbd2-5fc1a14018ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+x+1)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318517} {:answer/id #uuid "6dce171a-f262-55e9-a989-886e508e6d6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+x+1)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dce171a-f262-55e9-a989-886e508e6d6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+x+1)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318518} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6dd210f-83a2-5452-af92-c74dc577a8c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318513}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf0ee7c6-880a-54c4-8a1b-65046887b422" :question/math-academy-id "q-49873" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+2x+1}{x({x}^{2}+x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a negative discriminant:\n\n$$\nD={1}^{2}-4(1)(1)=-3<0\n$$\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}+2x+1}{x({x}^{2}+x+1)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{Bx+C}{{x}^{2}+x+1}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $x({x}^{2}+x+1),$ and we get\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}+2x+1=A({x}^{2}+x+1)+(Bx+C)x.\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=1,B=2,$ and $C=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}+2x+1}{x({x}^{2}+x+1)}=\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x+1}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+2x+1}{x({x}^{2}+x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x+1}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}+x+1.$ Then $\\text{d}u=(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+x+1| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+2x+1}{x({x}^{2}+x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+x+1)+K\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c22b8e9-049a-5574-86c9-35788c410421" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Binomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d484f9ee-57ab-52bd-80b7-1f50124a4ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\ln \\mid x - 1 \\mid + 2\\ln (x^{2} + 1) - \\arctan x + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067440} {:answer/id #uuid "e1407c9d-8481-5f14-8670-7336d116d474" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln \\mid x - 1 \\mid + \\ln (x^{2} + 1) + \\arctan x + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067441} {:answer/id #uuid "20d92852-618a-5a8a-adca-fa9d1c995e94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln \\mid x - 1 \\mid - \\frac{1}{2}\\ln (x^{2} + 1) - \\arctan x + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067442} {:answer/id #uuid "28fcb450-478d-515f-b8c4-d44949c70ac9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\ln \\mid x - 1 \\mid - \\frac{1}{4}\\ln (x^{2} + 1) + \\arctan x + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067443} {:answer/id #uuid "776b016d-3417-559e-9e97-bc186239e976" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln \\mid x - 1 \\mid - \\ln (x^{2} + 1) + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20d92852-618a-5a8a-adca-fa9d1c995e94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln \\mid x - 1 \\mid - \\frac{1}{2}\\ln (x^{2} + 1) - \\arctan x + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067442} :answer-field/id #uuid "7396243b-a391-55d7-934f-905961ca56c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d605be2d-ae71-5e50-9bf1-07465ceead87" :question/math-academy-id "q-49919" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int \\frac{2}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+1)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The quadratic factor ${x}^{2}+1$ is irreducible, so we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+1)}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{Bx+C}{{x}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-1)({x}^{2}+1),$ and we get\n\n$$\n2=A({x}^{2}+1)+(Bx+C)(x-1).\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=1,B=-1,$ and $C=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+1)}=\\frac{1}{x-1}+\\frac{-x-1}{{x}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x-1}+\\frac{-x-1}{{x}^{2}+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}+1.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+1| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+K\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318519 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a78860ea-192f-5df9-aca9-4f67ec6ffefe" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Given Part Of the Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d36d4433-ae57-59c7-a79d-faccd9a7c6b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4|+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318521} {:answer/id #uuid "d3dfb24a-12f8-5aaa-8e62-47104b086053" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318522} {:answer/id #uuid "ee2b13e4-0137-5003-bd9c-dc9bdfa5ea3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318523} {:answer/id #uuid "4fc079d8-01e1-502c-8199-37fe7d0455be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318524} {:answer/id #uuid "93a2363d-e98a-5d1c-b5c9-40043284fff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93a2363d-e98a-5d1c-b5c9-40043284fff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318525} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c1b1ff3-a156-5663-a350-0131dd0fc6d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3384891-25a4-5406-9453-8b9c2d2bdd39" :question/math-academy-id "q-83161" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+3}{({x}^{2}+4)(x-1)}=\\frac{Ax+1}{{x}^{2}+4}+\\frac{1}{x-1},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant to be found, calculate $\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x+3}{({x}^{2}+4)(x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the constant $A.$ Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+4)(x-1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x+3 & =(Ax+1)(x-1)+{x}^{2}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2$  into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2}+2+3 & =(A(2)+1)(2-1)+{2}^{2}+4 \\\\ 9 & =2A+1+8 \\\\ 9 & =2A+9 \\\\ A & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x+3}{({x}^{2}+4)(x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{0x+1}{{x}^{2}+4}+\\frac{1}{x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x+3}{({x}^{2}+4)(x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318526 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Trinomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2952684-53b5-5341-b122-aacc9daa90d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-x+2)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318528} {:answer/id #uuid "92e3dbf6-0390-5a57-89c7-ab92c91266fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-x+2)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318529} {:answer/id #uuid "9b4866af-c6e4-5a0d-852a-c0a314911817" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}-x+2}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318530} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3028bf-9957-57b4-a580-c7b5c6e0d6f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-x+2)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318531} {:answer/id #uuid "fd22addd-d1c0-5fed-9461-55d44c50c346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-x+2}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92e3dbf6-0390-5a57-89c7-ab92c91266fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-x+2)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318529} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6784886-a59f-5a67-bc6b-39641c1f2b00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "15e6d5a7-8c5f-5492-a86f-28b4cc21cf31" :question/math-academy-id "q-83230" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}-3x+4}{x({x}^{2}-x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a negative discriminant:\n\n$$\nD=(-1)^{2}-4(1)(2)=-7<0\n$$\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-3x+4}{x({x}^{2}-x+2)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{Bx+C}{{x}^{2}-x+2}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $x({x}^{2}-x+2),$ and we get\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-3x+4=A({x}^{2}-x+2)+(Bx+C)x.\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=2,B=2,$ and $C=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-3x+4}{x({x}^{2}-x+2)}=\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}-x+2}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{2}-3x+4}{x({x}^{2}-x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}-x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}-x+2}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}-x+2.$ Then $\\text{d}u=(2x-1)\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}-x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-x+2| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}-3x+4}{x({x}^{2}-x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}-x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-x+2)+K\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318533 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a78860ea-192f-5df9-aca9-4f67ec6ffefe" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Given Part Of the Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "243b348a-9515-565f-a6ca-a045773709c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318535} {:answer/id #uuid "904b2345-1ba1-5c96-a736-c4660f23f437" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3)+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318536} {:answer/id #uuid "c9002024-9abc-51fe-b4ad-97ccf7355eb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318537} {:answer/id #uuid "8e6e4b35-16b5-5990-a6f8-4e144b06fdf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3)+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318538} {:answer/id #uuid "0f9942f6-6259-5af5-93ab-e860860d5426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3)-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9002024-9abc-51fe-b4ad-97ccf7355eb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318537} :answer-field/id #uuid "3665db69-ec8b-5113-be2f-9fd3b0b0f350" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9eb43c75-f26e-52b2-8738-8026f1d35ba3" :question/math-academy-id "q-86124" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}+4x+3}{({x}^{2}+3)(x+2)}=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+3}+\\frac{D}{x+2},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant to be found, calculate $\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+4x+3}{({x}^{2}+3)(x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the constant $D.$ Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+3)(x+2)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+4x+3 & =2x(x+2)+D({x}^{2}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-2$  into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-2)^{2}+4(-2)+3 & =2(-2)(-2+2)+D((-2)^{2}+3) \\\\ 7 & =7D \\\\ D & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+4x+3}{({x}^{2}+3)(x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+3}+\\frac{1}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution ${x}^{2}+3=u.$ Then, $2x\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+3| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+4x+3}{({x}^{2}+3)(x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+3)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
